h, which rounds ingress and egress to a bin.\",\"Flux is kept to 1 ppm and its error to 5 ppm.\",\"Normalized by the median. Lomb-Scargle with the error bars as weights (astropy.timeseries.LombScargle), ten samples per peak between 0.5 day and the longest period; false-alarm probability by the naive formula for the number of independent frequencies.\",\"Box least squares (astropy.timeseries.BoxLeastSquares), durations 1 to 6 hours, a coarse grid then a fine grid across the best peak, scored by the likelihood; the epoch of the best box is barycentric Julian date 2459826.78542 (TDB).\",\"The depth's sigma is the box search's, rescaled by the box model's reduced chi-square when it exceeds 1; the signal-to-noise ratio is the depth over that sigma.\"],\"retrieved\":\"2026-09-24\",\"source\":{\"id\":\"pack:tess-hd209458-s56-lc@1.0.0\",\"kind\":\"import\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\"},\"title\":\"HD 209458: TESS sector 56 light curve: Lomb-Scargle and box least squares on one period axis\"}"}